MiOS Hypr3D rotated outputs (applies after hypr3d-mios-retina-spawn.patch). On an output with a transform
(portrait by rotation, flips) the room rendered in the panel buffer's orientation and sampled window snapshots
Hyprland had rendered through the transform: it showed sideways with the wrong window content (measured: status
size=1080x1920 pixel=1920x1080 scene=3840x2160, a 900x560 window drawn as a 476x764 white slab). Now:

- the scene renders upright (the output's logical orientation, aspect W_t / H_t, SSAA at m_transformedSize x
  render.scale) and the composite maps it into the buffer through the output transform (the blit's UV); the
  typing-mode pointer follows through the same map; the crosshair is symmetric and stays in buffer space;
- every snapshot (window, popup, layer, the wallpaper dome, each tile of an oversized window) is copied upright
  once after capture, so UVs, texSpan, mipmaps and the outline tracer see the logical orientation;
- pixel densities (tiled capture, outline and layer alpha masks) use m_transformedSize.

The map from buffer to upright texture coordinates for wl_output_transform t is M_t (0 (x, y), 1 (-y, x),
2 (-x, -y), 3 (y, -x), 4 (-x, y), 5 (y, x), 6 (x, -y), 7 (-y, -x)), measured in nested sessions for all eight
transforms (window at the work-area centre at 1:1, a second window cascaded right/down). A normal output
(transform 0) takes exactly the old code paths. Cost on a rotated output: one extra full-snapshot draw per capture
(capture rates and counts unchanged).

